{"name":"Little Valley","hex":"#a4a191","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Little Valley","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A census-designated place in Lassen County, California, United States.","A township in McPherson County, Kansas, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Little_Valley"}],"entries":[{"title":"Little Valley, California","blocks":[{"text":"Little Valley is an unincorporated community and census-designated place in Lassen County, California, United States. It is located 43 miles (69 km) northwest of Susanville, at an elevation of 4,190 feet (1,280 m). Its population is 84 as of the 2020 census."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Lassen_County_California_Incorporated_and_Unincorporated_areas_Little_Valley_Highlighted_0641908.svg/330px-Lassen_County_California_Incorporated_and_Unincorporated_areas_Little_Valley_Highlighted_0641908.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Valley%2C_California","wikidata":"Q6652380"},{"title":"Little Valley Township, Kansas","blocks":[{"text":"Little Valley Township is a township in McPherson County, Kansas, United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Map_highlighting_Little_Valley_Township%2C_McPherson_County%2C_Kansas.svg/330px-Map_highlighting_Little_Valley_Township%2C_McPherson_County%2C_Kansas.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Valley_Township%2C_Kansas","wikidata":"Q9041621"},{"title":"Valley","blocks":[{"text":"A valley is an elongated low area often running between hills or mountains and typically containing a river or stream running from one end to the other. Most valleys are formed by erosion of the land surface by rivers or streams over a very long period. Some valleys are formed through erosion by glacial i